      "writtenOn": "2026-10-28T00:55:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Would it be possible to do the zero-page sibling reuse inside `p3s_wp_install_folio_slices()`?\n\n`wp_page_copy()` already calls it and jumps to `pte_installed` when it returns true, and today it returns false for the zero page, so it could look around, zero the slice, add the rmap and set the PTE itself.\n\n`wp_page_copy()` would then stay as it is after Batch 10",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "5f1a285d5594ae3ef4ac89dc636466c13021477f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a710b6cf_5e6a807e",
        "filename": "mm/memory.c",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 3944,
      "author": {
        "id": 1499410
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-28T00:55:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this bypasses the rmap by bumping `_mapcount` directly.\n\nIn a `VM_LOCKED` VMA the folio would then miss this slice\u0027s `mlock_folio()`, so it could be munlocked while the VMA still maps a slice of it, for example after `mlock()` of a range whose zero-page PTEs were read first (mlock populates with write faults). Batch 10 removed this kind of raw increment from `p3s_anon_folio_reuse()` for the same reason.\n\nCould this use `folio_add_anon_rmap_pte(new_folio, \u0026new_folio-\u003epage, vma, vmf-\u003eaddress, RMAP_NONE)` instead?",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "5f1a285d5594ae3ef4ac89dc636466c13021477f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
